Design a class in Java to build a Balanced Binary Search Tree with the following constraints: the height of the tree should not exceed log2(n), where n is the number of elements in the tree, and the average search time for an element should be O(log n). Additionally, the class should support the following operations:
- Insertion of elements with a time complexity of O(log n)
- Deletion of elements with a time complexity of O(log n)
- Finding the kth smallest element in the tree with a time complexity of O(log n)
- Finding the largest element in the tree with a time complexity of O(log n)
- Merging two Balanced Binary Search Trees into one with a time complexity of O(log(n1 + n2)), where n1 and n2 are the number of elements in the two trees respectively.

