### Instruction:
Generate a Java program that prints the longest palindrome word in a sentence, considering that the sentence may contain multiple palindrome words with the same length. If there are multiple longest palindrome words, the program should print all of them. Additionally, the program should ignore any punctuation marks and whitespace characters when checking for palindromes.

### Response:
Here is a Java program that finds and prints the longest palindrome word(s) in a sentence, ignoring punctuation marks and whitespace characters:

```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class LongestPalindrome {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String sentence = "A man, a plan, a canal, Panama!";
        List<String> longestPalindromes = findLongestPalindromeWords(sentence);

        System.out.println("Longest palindrome word(s):");
        for (String palindrome : longestPalindromes) {
            System.out.println(palindrome);
        }
    }

    public static List<String> findLongestPalindromeWords(String sentence) {
        List<String> palindromeWords = new ArrayList<>();
        String[] words = sentence.split("\\W+"); // Split sentence into words ignoring punctuation marks and whitespace

        int maxLength = 0;
        for (String word : words) {
            if (isPalindrome(word)) {
                int length = word.length();
                if (length > maxLength) {
                    maxLength = length;
                    palindromeWords.clear();
                    palindromeWords.add(word);
                } else if (length == maxLength) {
                    palindromeWords.add(word);
                }
            }
        }

        return palindromeWords;
    }

    public static boolean isPalindrome(String word) {
        int left = 0;
        int right = word.length() - 1;

        while (left < right) {
            if (word.charAt(left) != word.charAt(right)) {
                return false;
            }
            left++;
            right--;
        }

        return true;
    }
}
```

Output:
