### Response:
To solve the problem with a time complexity of O(nlogn) and without using additional data structures or arrays, we can implement the Patience Sorting algorithm. This algorithm simulates a card game called Patience, where the goal is to create piles of cards in increasing order.

Here's the updated code:

```csharp
public static int LongestIncreasingSubsequence(int[] arr)
{
    int n = arr.Length;
    int[] top = new int[n];
    int piles = 0;

    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        // Binary search to find the correct pile to place the current element
        int left = 0;
        int right = piles;

        while (left < right)
        {
            int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;
            if (arr[i] > arr[top[mid]])
            {
                left = mid + 1;
            }
            else
            {
                right = mid;
            }
        }

        // Place the current element in the correct pile
        if (left == piles)
        {
            piles++;
        }
        top[left] = i;
    }

    return piles;
}
```

The algorithm uses the "top" array to keep track of the smallest ending value of each pile. By the end of the algorithm, the number of piles will be the length of the longest increasing subsequence.

The time complexity of this algorithm is O(nlogn) because the binary search is performed for each element in the array, and the binary search has a time complexity of O(logn).

### Instruction:
Create a singly linked list in Java and add the following elements: 5, 7, 3, 9, 2, 6. Sort the linked list in descending order using a merge sort algorithm and then print the elements in reverse order.

### Response:
Here's an example of creating a singly linked list in Java, adding the given elements, sorting it in descending order using merge sort algorithm, and then printing the elements in reverse order:

```java
class Node {
    int data;
    Node next;

    public Node(int data) {
        this.data = data;
        this.next = null;
    }
}

class LinkedList {
    Node head;

    public LinkedList() {
        this.head = null;
    }

    public void insert(int data) {
        Node newNode = new Node(data);
        if (head == null) {
            head = newNode;
        } else {
            Node current = head;
            while (current.next != null) {
                current = current.next;
            }
            current.next = newNode;
        }
    }

    public void mergeSort() {
        head = mergeSort(head);
    }

    private Node mergeSort(Node node) {
        if (node == null || node.next == null) {
            return node;
        }

        Node middle = getMiddle(node);
        Node nextOfMiddle = middle.next;
        middle.next = null;

        Node left = mergeSort(node);
        Node right = mergeSort(nextOfMiddle);

        return merge(left, right);
    }

    private Node merge(Node left, Node right) {
        Node result = null;

        if (left == null) {
            return right;
        }
        if (right == null) {
            return left;
        }

        if (left.data >= right.data) {
            result = left;
            result.next = merge(left.next, right);
        } else {
            result = right;
            result.next = merge(left, right.next);
        }
        return result;
    }

    private Node getMiddle(Node node) {
        if (node == null) {
            return node;
        }

        Node slow = node;
        Node fast = node;

        while (fast.next != null && fast.next.next != null) {
            slow = slow.next;
            fast = fast.next.next;
        }

        return slow;
    }

    public void printReverse() {
        printReverse(head);
    }

    private void printReverse(Node node) {
        if (node == null) {
            return;
        }
        printReverse(node.next);
        System.out.print(node.data + " ");
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        LinkedList list = new LinkedList();
        list.insert(5);
        list.insert(7);
        list.insert(3);
        list.insert(9);
        list.insert(2);
        list.insert(6);

        System.out.println("Original List:");
        list.printReverse();

        list.mergeSort();

        System.out.println("\nSorted List in Descending Order:");
        list.printReverse();
    }
}
```

