### Response:
Here is an example Java class that implements a binary search algorithm to search for the target element in a sorted array of integers:

```java
public class BinarySearch {
    public static int binarySearch(int[] arr, int target) {
        int left = 0;
        int right = arr.length - 1;

        while (left <= right) {
            int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;

            if (arr[mid] == target) {
                // Check if the target element is the first occurrence
                while (mid > 0 && arr[mid - 1] == target) {
                    mid--;
                }
                return mid;
            }

            if (arr[mid] < target) {
                left = mid + 1;
            } else {
                right = mid - 1;
            }
        }

        // Element not found
