console.log(isSortedAndUnique([1, 2, 3, 4, 4])); // Output: false
console.log(isSortedAndUnique([1, 3, 2, 4, 5])); // Output: false
```

This algorithm uses a merge sort algorithm to sort the array in ascending order, which has a time complexity of O(nlogn). After sorting the array, it checks if there are any duplicate elements by comparing each element with its adjacent element. If any duplicates are found, the function returns false. Otherwise, it returns true.

