### Instruction:
Write a C# code snippet to create a binary search tree with the following string payload and print it out. However, you are not allowed to use the built-in BinarySearchTree<T> class or any other built-in tree data structure. You must implement your own custom data structure to store and retrieve the strings using the binary search tree algorithm. Additionally, the code must handle duplicate strings by either discarding them or storing them in a separate data structure for later retrieval.

### Response:
Here is an example of how you can create a binary search tree with string payload without using the built-in BinarySearchTree<T> class in C#:

```csharp
using System;

public class BinarySearchTree
{
    public class Node
    {
        public string Payload;
        public Node Left;
        public Node Right;

        public Node(string payload)
        {
            Payload = payload;
            Left = null;
            Right = null;
        }
    }

    private Node Root;

    public BinarySearchTree()
    {
        Root = null;
    }

    public void Insert(string payload)
    {
        if (Root == null)
        {
            Root = new Node(payload);
            return;
        }

        Node currentNode = Root;

        while (true)
        {
            if (string.Compare(payload, currentNode.Payload) < 0)
            {
                if (currentNode.Left == null)
                {
                    currentNode.Left = new Node(payload);
                    break;
                }
                else
                {
                    currentNode = currentNode.Left;
                }
            }
            else if (string.Compare(payload, currentNode.Payload) > 0)
            {
                if (currentNode.Right == null)
                {
                    currentNode.Right = new Node(payload);
                    break;
                }
                else
                {
                    currentNode = currentNode.Right;
                }
            }
            else
            {
                // Handle duplicates here
                break;
            }
        }
    }

    private void InOrderTraversal(Node node)
    {
        if (node != null)
        {
            InOrderTraversal(node.Left);
            Console.WriteLine(node.Payload);
            InOrderTraversal(node.Right);
        }
    }

    public void Print()
    {
        InOrderTraversal(Root);
    }
}

public class Program
{
    public static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        BinarySearchTree bst = new BinarySearchTree();
        bst.Insert("apple");
        bst.Insert("banana");
        bst.Insert("apple");
        bst.Insert("cherry");
        bst.Insert("banana");
        bst.Insert("date");

        bst.Print();
    }
}
```

This code creates a custom BinarySearchTree class with a nested Node class. The Insert method is used to insert strings into the tree, and the Print method performs an in-order traversal of the tree to print out the strings in ascending order. The code also handles duplicate strings by discarding them. In the Main method, a sample tree is created and printed out.

